course: dictionary
lesson: 14065
title: Words about mothers and families
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Maternal is a word about mothers. When you see it, ask yourself: is this about a mother, or about something a mother does? Look at the words around it for clues.
explain: «My maternal grandmother lives in the village.» Maternal tells you which side of the family she is from. She is your mum's mother, so she is on your mum's side.
explain: «The hen showed maternal care, sitting on her eggs every day.» Maternal care is the caring a mother gives her young. The clues are sitting on eggs and every day, so it is caring like a mother.
fact: Maternal means to do with a mother, or being a mother.
fact: «Maternal grandfather» means your mum's dad.
fact: «Maternal health» means the health of women who are having babies.
fact: «Maternal instinct» is the caring feeling many mothers have towards their children.
fact: The word for the father's side is paternal, so maternal and paternal are opposites.
exercise: «My maternal grandmother lives in the village.» Who is she? | *Your mum's mother | Your cousin from school | Your dad's sister
exercise: «The hen showed maternal care, sitting on her eggs every day.» What does maternal care mean here? | Giving food away to strangers | *The care a mother gives her young | Care given by a teacher at school
exercise: Which phrase is about the health of women who are having babies? | maternal grandfather | a maternal fish | *maternal health
test: Jayden says maternal means "about dads". What does it really mean? | *To do with a mother or being a mother | To do with a father or being a father | To do with school dinners
test: Mia says «maternal instinct» means a love of maths. What does it really mean? | A love of numbers | *A caring feeling many mothers have for their children | A way to draw a map
exam: «Ella's maternal grandfather is her mum's dad.» Who is Ella's maternal grandfather? | Her teacher at school | Her dad's dad | *Her mum's dad
